### Identity API Documentation
### Complete API documentation for identity document management endpoints
### All operations for uploading, viewing, and managing user identity documents
### Reviewed and verified against implementation

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@contentType = application/json
@token = your-jwt-token-here

### ============================================
### VARIABLES SETUP
### ============================================
### Replace the variables above with actual values:
### - @token: JWT token from /api/auth/verify-otp

### ============================================
### 1. GET MY IDENTITY
### ============================================
### Get the authenticated user's identity documents and verification status
### Requires user JWT token

GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me/identity
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Response Example (200 OK):
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Identity fetched successfully",
###   "data": {
###     "id": "identity-uuid",
###     "userId": "user-uuid",
###     "isVerified": false,
###     "verifiedBy": null,
###     "images": [
###       "https://ajwadi.s3.eu-west-3.amazonaws.com/identity/...",
###       "https://ajwadi.s3.eu-west-3.amazonaws.com/identity/..."
###     ],
###     "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
###     "updatedAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
###   }
### }

### Response Example (404 Not Found):
### {
###   "success": false,
###   "message": "Identity not found"
### }

### ============================================
### 2. UPLOAD/UPDATE MY IDENTITY
### ============================================
### Upload or update identity documents for the authenticated user
### Requires user JWT token
### File upload is REQUIRED
### If identity already exists, it will be updated (verification status will be reset)

### STEP 1: Get Upload URL for Identity Document(s)
### You can upload multiple identity documents (front, back, etc.)

POST {{baseUrl}}/s3/upload-url
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "fileName": "identity-front.jpg",
  "fileType": "image",
  "filePurpose": "identity"
}

### Response Example:
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "data": {
###     "uploadUrl": "https://ajwadi.s3.eu-west-3.amazonaws.com/identity/...",
###     "file": {
###       "id": "file-uuid-here",
###       "fileName": "identity-front.jpg",
###       "fileType": "image",
###       "filePurpose": "identity",
###       "url": "https://ajwadi.s3.eu-west-3.amazonaws.com/identity/...",
###       ...
###     },
###     "uploadToken": "token-string-here"
###   }
### }

### Repeat Step 1 for additional identity documents (e.g., back side)

POST {{baseUrl}}/s3/upload-url
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "fileName": "identity-back.jpg",
  "fileType": "image",
  "filePurpose": "identity"
}

### STEP 2: Upload Files to S3
### Use the uploadUrl from Step 1 to upload the actual files
### This is a PUT request to the signed URL (not to our API)
### Note: Replace {{uploadUrl}} with the actual URL from Step 1 response

PUT {{uploadUrl}}
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./path/to/your/identity-front.jpg

### Repeat for additional files

PUT {{uploadUrl}}
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./path/to/your/identity-back.jpg

### STEP 3: Upload/Update Identity
### After uploading files to S3, use the fileId, uploadToken, and purpose from Step 1
### IMPORTANT: identityPicture must be an array, even for single files
### You can include multiple identity documents in one request

POST {{baseUrl}}/users/me/identity
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "identityPicture": [
    {
      "fileId": "file-uuid-from-step-1-front",
      "token": "token-from-step-1-front",
      "purpose": "identity"
    },
    {
      "fileId": "file-uuid-from-step-1-back",
      "token": "token-from-step-1-back",
      "purpose": "identity"
    }
  ]
}

### Example with single identity document:
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/me/identity
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "identityPicture": [
    {
      "fileId": "file-uuid-here",
      "token": "token-here",
      "purpose": "identity"
    }
  ]
}

### Response Example (201 Created - New Identity):
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Identity documents uploaded successfully. Verification pending.",
###   "data": {
###     "id": "identity-uuid",
###     "userId": "user-uuid",
###     "isVerified": false,
###     "verifiedBy": null,
###     "images": [
###       "https://ajwadi.s3.eu-west-3.amazonaws.com/identity/...",
###       "https://ajwadi.s3.eu-west-3.amazonaws.com/identity/..."
###     ],
###     "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
###     "updatedAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
###   }
### }

### Response Example (200 OK - Updated Identity):
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Identity documents updated successfully. Verification pending.",
###   "data": {
###     "id": "identity-uuid",
###     "userId": "user-uuid",
###     "isVerified": false,
###     "verifiedBy": null,
###     "images": [
###       "https://ajwadi.s3.eu-west-3.amazonaws.com/identity/...",
###       "https://ajwadi.s3.eu-west-3.amazonaws.com/identity/..."
###     ],
###     "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
###     "updatedAt": "2024-01-01T00:05:00.000Z"
###   }
### }

### Error Response (Missing Files):
### {
###   "success": false,
###   "message": "At least one identity document file is required"
### }

### Error Response (Invalid File):
### {
###   "success": false,
###   "message": "No valid files found"
### }

### Error Response (File Not Ready):
### {
###   "success": false,
###   "message": "Files are not ready yet"
### }

### ============================================
### COMPREHENSIVE NOTES & GUIDELINES
### ============================================

### 1. AUTHENTICATION & AUTHORIZATION
###    - All endpoints require user JWT token
###    - Users can only access their own identity documents
###    - Include Authorization header: Authorization: Bearer <your-jwt-token>

### 2. FILE UPLOAD FLOW
###    - Step 1: Get upload URL from /api/s3/upload-url
###    - Step 2: Upload file to S3 using the signed URL (PUT request)
###    - Step 3: Use fileId, token, and purpose in the identity upload request
###    - File upload tokens are required for security and validation
###    - Purpose must match: "identity" for identity documents

### 3. IDENTITY DOCUMENTS
###    - You can upload multiple identity documents (front, back, etc.)
###    - All documents must be uploaded to S3 before submitting
###    - Supported file types: images (jpg, png, etc.)
###    - File purpose must be "identity"

### 4. VERIFICATION STATUS
###    - When identity is uploaded/updated, isVerified is set to false
###    - Verification is done by employees/admins
###    - verifiedBy field stores the employee ID who verified the identity
###    - Updating identity documents resets the verification status

### 5. VALIDATION RULES
###    - identityPicture: Required, must be an array
###    - Each file reference must include: fileId, token, purpose
###    - At least one identity document is required
###    - Files must be uploaded to S3 and ready before submission

### 6. ERROR RESPONSES
###    - 400 Bad Request: Missing files, invalid file references, files not ready
###    - 401 Unauthorized: Missing or invalid authentication token
###    - 404 Not Found: Identity not found (for GET request)
###    - 500 Internal Server Error: Server error

### 7. USAGE EXAMPLES

### Example 1: Upload Single Identity Document
### (After uploading file to S3)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/me/identity
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "identityPicture": [
    {
      "fileId": "identity-file-uuid",
      "token": "identity-upload-token",
      "purpose": "identity"
    }
  ]
}

### Example 2: Upload Multiple Identity Documents
### (After uploading files to S3)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/me/identity
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "identityPicture": [
    {
      "fileId": "identity-front-uuid",
      "token": "identity-front-token",
      "purpose": "identity"
    },
    {
      "fileId": "identity-back-uuid",
      "token": "identity-back-token",
      "purpose": "identity"
    }
  ]
}

### Example 3: Get Identity Status
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me/identity
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. BEST PRACTICES
###    - Upload clear, high-quality images of identity documents
###    - Include both front and back of identity documents when applicable
###    - Ensure files are fully uploaded to S3 before submitting
###    - Keep identity documents secure and private
###    - Update identity documents if they expire or change

### 9. SECURITY NOTES
###    - File upload tokens are required to prevent unauthorized file associations
###    - Tokens have expiration times for security
###    - Users can only upload/update their own identity documents
###    - Identity documents are stored securely in S3
###    - Verification status prevents unauthorized access

### 10. INTEGRATION NOTES
###     - Identity is created during user registration (required for freelancers)
###     - Identity can be updated after registration using this endpoint
###     - Updating identity resets verification status
###     - Employees can verify identity documents through admin endpoints
###     - Verified identity is required for certain platform features

### 11. FILE UPLOAD TOKEN FORMAT
###     When uploading files, use this format in the request body:
###     {
###       "identityPicture": [
###         {
###           "fileId": "uuid-from-s3-upload-url-response",
###           "token": "token-from-s3-upload-url-response",
###           "purpose": "identity"
###         }
###       ]
###     }
###     Note: Even for single files, it must be an array

### 12. IDENTITY VERIFICATION WORKFLOW
###     1. User uploads identity documents (isVerified: false)
###     2. Employee/admin reviews documents
###     3. Employee/admin verifies identity (isVerified: true, verifiedBy: employeeId)
###     4. If user updates identity, verification is reset (isVerified: false)
